(a) whether the recent successful semi-cryogenic engine power head test has advanced India's capability for future human spaceflight and deep-space missions;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether the semi-cryogenic engine is proposed to be utilized in future launch vehicles supporting Gaganyaan, Chandrayaan-4, Chandrayaan-5 and other heavy-lift missions;
(d) the present status of integration planning and technology validation for such missions; and
(e) the timeline envisaged for operational deployment of the technology in India's next-generation launch systems?

(a) whether Government has operationalised the Next Generation DNA Sequencing Facility and Digital Wildlife Information Systems for strengthening wildlife conservation and research;
(b) the objectives, expenditure incurred and major features of these facilities;
(c) whether these facilities would be used for genetic profiling, wildlife forensics, disease surveillance and monitoring of endangered species;
(d) whether the State Forest Departments and protected areas are proposed to be integrated with the digital platform; and
(e) the steps taken to promote technology-driven wildlife conservation, real-time data sharing and capacity building across the country?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any review of digitization and digital archival management initiatives of the National Archives of India through the 'Abhilekh Patal' platform;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the details of progress made under the platform with regard to digitization, metadata standardization and expansion of digital archival repository; 
(d) whether measures have been taken to strengthen digital accessibility, archival search capabilities and integration of emerging technologies to improve public access to archival records; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the current status of nationwide rollout of Advanced Postal Technology platform under the IT Modernisation Project 2.0 across Post Offices and Postal Circles;
(b) the details of digital tools, including the Digital Rural Enterprise Application for Mobiles (DREAM) App, provided to Postmen and Gramin Dak Sevaks to strengthen doorstep banking and rural service delivery;
(c) whether any institutional framework exists for integrating India Post’s logistics and financial services with e-commerce and last-mile delivery;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the roadmap for modernising post offices nationwide and enhancing citizen-facing digital services under India Post’s transformation plan?

(a) the operational status of Kalpakkam Mini Reactor (KAMINI) including its licensing position with the Atomic Energy Regulatory Board;
(b) whether life-extension measures are being undertaken for KAMINI, as it nears three decades of service;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) the research applications supported by KAMINI, including fission chamber testing and detector calibration and whether any mechanism exists for BARC-IGCAR collaboration on utilising its facilities;
(e) whether any roadmap exists for KAMINI’s role in supporting the third stage of India’s nuclear power programme in the coming years; and
(f) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of children successfully adopted through Central Adoption Resource Authority (CARA) during Financial Year 2025-26, the State-wise details thereof;
(b) the number of specialized adoption agencies strengthened or newly registered during the said period;
(c) the measures taken to reduce the average time taken to complete the adoption processes; and
(d) the further steps proposed to expand awareness and access to adoption services?

(a) whether the Ministry has unveiled 'PRAHAAR' as India's first comprehensive 'National Counter-Terrorism Policy and Strategy,' and if so, the date of unveiling and the key pillars thereof;
(b) the specific objectives of 'PRAHAAR' that could not be effectively addressed under the existing counter-terrorism and internal security framework;
(c) the institutional and coordination mechanisms proposed between Central and State agencies for the implementation of this policy; and
(d) the timeline for the operationalization of this strategy and the manner in which the outcomes thereof would be reviewed?

(a) the status of the implementation of digital toll collection initiatives on the National Highways;
(b) the information regarding measures undertaken to facilitate technology-enabled toll collection on the National Highway network;
(c) whether the Ministry is planning  to expand barrier-free electronic toll collection; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether preparatory activities for Census 2027, including House Listing and Housing Census, have commenced across all States and Union Territories;
(b) the State-wise status of digital infrastructure and self-enumeration facilities for Census, 2027;
(c) whether training programmes have been conducted for census functionaries and supervisors;
(d) whether any funds have been released to States and Union Territories for census-related activities; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the objectives and salient features of the Prime Minister Research Chair (PMRC) scheme 2026 launched to attract accomplished Indian-origin researchers and scientists to Indian institutions;
(b) the number of Lead Institutions and Host Institutions identified so far under the scheme and the thematic areas of national priority covered;
(c) the number of applications received from Fellows and Host Institutions since opening of the portal, and the selection process being followed; and
(d) the financial outlay earmarked for the scheme and the manner in which it is expected to strengthen India's research and innovation ecosystem?

(a) whether Government is aware that several CGHS-empanelled private hospitals have reportedly restricted or discontinued cashless treatment facilities due to delays in reimbursement of CGHS claims;
(b) if so, the total amount of reimbursement claims pending as on date, State-wise and hospital-wise, along with the reasons for such pendency;
(c) the average and maximum time taken for settlement of CGHS claims during the last three years; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to ensure time-bound reimbursement to hospitals and the timeline fixed for clearing all pending dues?

(a) the State-wise and gender-wise progress achieved under the Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY) and Jan Suraksha Schemes, including the cumulative number of beneficiaries as of June 2026;
(b) the total credit disbursed under the Pradhan Mantri MUDRA Yojana (PMMY), including the category-wise distribution among SC, ST, OBC and women entrepreneurs;
(c) the measures taken to ensure the quality and sustainability of MUDRA lending, including the trend in non-performing assets (NPAs); and
(d) the progress made under the Tarun Plus category, including the number and value of loans sanctioned and its contribution towards supporting growth-oriented micro enterprises?

(a) whether Government has taken note of the wide variation in maximum retail prices (MRPs) of medicines containing the same active pharmaceutical ingredient (salt), strength and dosage form but sold under different brand names, if so, the details thereof and the reasons for such variations;
(b) whether any study has been conducted on the extent of such price differences and their impact on patients’ out-of-pocket expenditure, if so, the findings thereof;
(c) whether Government proposes to regulate and rationalise such MRPs through appropriate guidelines, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen monitoring and ensure affordable access to medicines?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any recent review regarding the expansion of PNG and CNG infrastructure and fuel supply networks in the State of Maharashtra;
(b) if so, the details of domestic PNG connections, CNG stations and pipeline infrastructure added in the State during the last three years and the current year; and
(c) the targets fixed for further expansion and the timeline for achieving universal access in eligible urban and semi-urban areas in the State of Maharashtra?

(a) the specific steps taken by the Ministry to improve 'Ease of Doing Business', including reforms in labour, land taxation, insolvency and the impact on India’s ranking in global indices;
(b) the current status of export growth and the measures adopted to achieve the target of $2 trillion exports;
(c) the details of new markets and products identified for export promotion; and
(d) the details of support provided to Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) and exporters for overcoming challenges in international trade?

(a) whether Government has taken note of reports indicating that India is among the countries experiencing the highest agricultural yield losses due to human-induced land degradation, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the extent of agricultural land affected by degradation, State-wise, including Maharashtra;
(c) whether any assessment has been undertaken regarding the impact of land degradation on crop productivity, farm incomes and food security; and
(d) the measures taken by the Centre to promote soil restoration, sustainable land management, water conservation and climate-resilient agriculture to reverse yield losses and improve agricultural productivity?

(a) whether Government is implementing the National Beekeeping and Honey Mission (NBHM);  
(b) if so, the  details and objectives thereof; and   
(c) the details of the steps taken/proposed to be taken by Government to increase honey production, scientific beekeeping and related advantages for agricultural productivity?

(a) the number of Central Government pensioners residing in Maharashtra and availing pension-related services;
(b) whether Government has received complaints regarding delays in pension processing and grievance redressal in the State;
(c) the number of grievances received and disposed of during the last three years; and
(d) the measures taken to improve digital pension services and the timeline for achieving complete online service delivery?

(a) the specific initiatives implemented to establish comprehensive wayside amenities along National Highways, encompassing rest areas, refreshment zones and rapid-response emergency facilities;
(b) the progress achieved in the electric vehicle charging infrastructure along high-traffic National Highway corridors during the last three years;
(c) whether the strategic adoption of Public-Private Partnership models for these facilities has successfully stimulated rural entrepreneurship and local economic growth;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the methodology through which trauma-care services and modern public-convenience infrastructure are being synchronised with the larger wayside amenities network?

(a) whether Government has initiated pilot projects for hydrogen-powered transport on ten selected highway corridors across the country, including the Pune–Mumbai route in Maharashtra;
(b) the details of the routes selected, objectives, implementing agencies and timelines for completion of the trials;
(c) whether any assessment has been made regarding the potential reduction in carbon emissions, fuel imports and operating costs through adoption of hydrogen-based mobility solutions; and
(d) the steps taken and funds allocated for developing hydrogen refuelling infrastructure and promoting green hydrogen transportation in Maharashtra and across the country?

(a) the current status of implementation regarding the five University Townships envisioned in the Union Budget 2026-27 near prominent industrial and logistics hubs;
(b) the framework through which these hubs seek to integrate academic institutions, research facilities and centres for skill development to enhance industry-academia synergy;
(c) the current status of the constitution of the High-Powered Standing Committee on Education to Employment and Enterprise and its core mandates;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the strategic initiatives undertaken to synchronise higher education to align with labour-market needs and improve the industry-readiness of graduates?

(a) the progress achieved under the "Sahakar se Samriddhi" vision in setting up new multipurpose Primary Agriculture Cooperative Credit Societies (PACS), dairy and fishery cooperative societies in previously unserved Gram Panchayats;
(b) whether the adoption of Model Bye-Laws has successfully empowered primary societies to expand their operational scope into diverse service-delivery domains;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the specific strategies formulated to bridge regional disparities and revitalise the cooperative movement in States where its presence is relatively low?

(a) whether Government has taken note of the number of complaints, representations and claim-related grievances received by the Deposit Insurance and Credit Guarantee Corporation(DICGC) during the last five years, bank-wise and State-wise;
(b) the total amount of insured deposits claimed, approved and disbursed to eligible depositors of failed, merged or restricted banks, year-wise and bank-wise;
(c) the number of depositors whose claims remain pending along with the amount yet to be paid and reasons for delay; and
(d) whether any timeline has been prescribed for settlement of pending claims and ensuring timely payment to depositors?

(a) whether Government has assessed the increasing incidence of urban flooding in major cities caused by inadequate storm-water drainage, encroachment of water bodies, unplanned urbanisation and extreme rainfall events and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the number of cities identified as highly vulnerable to urban flooding, State-wise; whether any city-wise assessment has been made of economic losses, infrastructure damage and disruption of public services during the last five years; and
(c) the measures taken, funds allocated and progress achieved in restoring water bodies, strengthening drainage networks, promoting flood-resilient urban planning and implementing early warning systems to mitigate urban flooding?

(a) whether Government proposes to promote Satellite-Based Landing System (SLS) approaches using the indigenous GAGAN system as an alternative or supplementary navigation aid to conventional ground-based systems, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the number of airports where GAGAN-enabled approach procedures have been approved, operationalised or are under implementation;
(c) whether regional and remote airports are proposed to be prioritised for deployment of GAGAN-enabled navigation facilities, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the funds allocated and targets fixed for expansion of GAGAN-based aviation infrastructure during the next three years?

(a) whether Government is aware of reports that large quantities of bedsheets, blankets, towels, pillows and other linen supplied in AC coaches have been stolen, causing significant financial losses to  Railways;
(b) total quantity and estimated value of such items reported missing and financial loss incurred during last five years, zone-wise;
(c) whether any assessment has been made regarding impact of these losses on passenger amenities and railway expenditure; 
(d)whether repeated shortage of linen has been flagged in internal audits/inspection reports, if so, the finding thereof and action taken thereon; and
(e) measures taken to prevent thefts, fix accountability and strengthen monitoring of linen inventory in trains?

(a) the details of the progress made under BHASHINI in the development of Artificial Intelligence (AI)-based language translation tools for Indian languages;
(b) the number of languages and dialects covered under the initiative so far and the number of datasets prepared therefor;
(c) whether Government has taken steps to integrate BHASHINI with Government service delivery platforms and e-Governance portals, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether Government has taken any steps to make digital content and services more accessible to non-English-speaking citizens, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of progress made in the implementation of the India-European Free Trade Association (EFTA) Trade and Economic Partnership Agreement (TEPA), including the investment commitments received under the agreement;
(b) the mechanism established to monitor the commitment of a 100 billion USD investment over a period of 15 years; and
(c) the details of steps taken to promote India's exports to EFTA countries?

(a) the number of applications received for appointment and renewal of Notary Certificates of Practice during the last five years, State-wise and district-wise;
(b) the number of applications approved, rejected and pending during the said period;
(c) whether delays have been reported in granting approvals and renewals and if so, the reasons therefor and the average time taken for disposal of applications;
(d) the number of Notary licences suspended or cancelled, State-wise and district-wise, along with the reasons therefor; and
(e) the measures taken to streamline and expedite the approval and renewal process?

(a) whether Government has introduced reforms to make passport services more accessible, efficient and citizen-centric and if so, the salient features thereof;
(b) the present status of implementation of e-Passports, including coverage achieved and the roadmap for phased expansion;
(c) whether steps have been taken to strengthen the network and service delivery of Passport Seva Kendras and Post Office Passport Seva Kendras, particularly in underserved areas; and
(d) the details of digital and technological interventions adopted to improve transparency, reduce processing time and enhance the overall passport service experience?

(a) whether it is a fact that advanced Avascular Necrosis (AVN) of the hip joint causes permanent mobility impairment and that certain premier institutions and Government hospitals have assessed eligible AVN cases under locomotor disability;
(b) if so, whether Government is aware of variations in the issuance of disability certificates to AVN patients by Medical Boards in Maharashtra and other States, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether Government has examined recognizing AVN as equivalent to locomotor disability under the RPwD Act, 2016 and proposes to issue uniform national guidelines and extend reservation and other admissible PwD benefits to eligible AVN patients?

(a) whether Government has taken cognizance of recent landslides, flooding and other monsoon-related incidents affecting the Mumbai–Goa Highway, Mumbai–Pune Expressway, Nashik Ring Road and other major road corridors in Maharashtra;
(b) district-wise details of damage caused to National Highways, expressways, bridges and related infrastructure in the State;
(c) the total financial loss assessed in Maharashtra due to such incidents; and
(d) the funds sanctioned, works undertaken and timeline fixed for restoration, slope-stabilisation and implementation of permanent safety measures on the affected stretches?

(a) the sanctioned strength, actual strength and vacancies in various Central Armed Police Forces (CAPFs) as on date;
(b) the Force-wise details thereof, including the Central Reserve Police Force, Border Security Force, Central Industrial Security Force, Indo-Tibetan Border Police and Sashastra Seema Bal; 
(c) the number of recruitments made during each of the last five years and the current year and State-wise breakup of such recruitments; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to fill vacancies and improve operational capacity of the Forces?

(a) the measures taken by Government for implementation of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 and the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023 across the country;
(b) the State-wise details of police personnel, prosecutors and judicial officers trained under the new criminal laws till date;
(c) the State-wise details of cases registered and disposed of under the new criminal laws since their implementation; and
(d) the details of digital platforms such as e-Sakshya, e-Summons and Nyaya Shruti integrated with the criminal justice system for implementation of the new laws?

