(a) the total number of schools selected under the PM SHRI Schools scheme as on date;
(b) the State-wise and Union Territory-wise details thereof;
(c) the details of funds allocated, released and utilised under the scheme during each of the last three years and the current year; and
(d) the measures taken to ensure that PM SHRI Schools emerge as exemplar institutions for implementation of the National Education Policy, 2020?

(a) the criteria and parameters adopted for the selection of Model Solar Villages under the PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijlee Yojana in the country, especially in Tripura, Jharkhand and Uttar Pradesh;
(b) the number of Model Solar Villages selected across the country and the progress achieved so far, State-wise including district-wise details of Tripura, Jharkhand and Uttar Pradesh;
(c) the financial assistance and other incentives provided by Government to promote the installation of rooftop solar systems in rural areas; and
(d) the manner in which the Model Solar Village initiative is contributing to rural energy access, clean energy adoption and sustainable development in the country including Tripura, Jharkhand and Uttar Pradesh?

(a) whether Government is aware that Maharashtra is establishing a state-of-the-art Health Emergency Operations Centre (HEOC) to strengthen preparedness for pandemics, disease outbreaks and public health emergencies, if so, the details thereof;  
(b) the total cost of the project, source of funding and assistance provided under the Pradhan Mantri Ayushman Bharat Health Infrastructure Mission (PM-ABHIM);  
(c) the details of surveillance, early-warning, data analytics and emergency response mechanisms proposed under the HEOC; and  
(d) whether similar centres are proposed in other States and Union Territories if so, the details and implementation timeline thereof, State/UT-wise?

(a) the financial performance metrics and Non-Performing Asset reductions recorded by Public Sector Banks (PSBs) over the last five years;
(b) the credit flow growth registered by PSBs toward the retail, agriculture, Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSME), and infrastructure sectors; and
(c) the total guarantee coverage and additional credit flow targeted specifically for the aviation sector under the Emergency Credit Line Guarantee Scheme (ECLGS 5.0)?

(a) the progress made in the 16 Research and Development projects being implemented under 'AYURGYAN' and the details of projects operated or approved State-wise;
(b) the operational status of Ayurveda Biology Integrated Health Research (ABIHR) component and the details of the research projects approved so far, collaborating institutions and key achievements under it, the details of the participation of institutions from Uttar Pradesh;
(c) the estimated timeline for establishing three new All India Institutes of Ayurveda (AIIA) announced in the 2026 Budget; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen research, education and healthcare infrastructure for promotion and integration of Ayurveda through these initiatives specially in Jharkhand?

(a) whether NITI Aayog is collaborating with Maharashtra for accelerating economic growth, innovation and regional development;
(b) if so, the details thereof including initiatives undertaken with Maharashtra Institution for Transformation (MITRA);
(c) the key outcomes achieved through such collaborations; and
(d) the future roadmap proposed for strengthening Centre-State cooperation in development planning and monitoring?

(a) the status of implementation of the 'deemed clearance' provisions under the Natural Gas and Petroleum Products Distribution (Through Laying, Building, Operation and Expansion of Pipelines and Other Facilities) Order, 2026; 
(b) the State-wise detail of regional pipeline networks expanding  from January, 2026 using standardized local body fee structures; 
(c) the manner in which Government is planning to resolve land access and right-of-way disputes through newly designated transparent dispute resolution authorities; 
(d) whether the newly launched time-bound approval framework has reduced the administrative pipeline expansion backlog in suburban residential areas; and 
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the need for accelerated expansion of PNG infrastructure to strengthen energy security and reduce dependence on LPG cylinders;
(b) the State-wise and city-wise status of domestic PNG coverage, including households connected and targets with timelines for achieving universal urban household coverage;
(c) whether demand for PNG connections in Pune and Pimpri-Chinchwad has increased and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the timeline and steps envisaged to achieve near 100 per cent PNG coverage through expedited last-mile connectivity and completion of pending pipeline networks?

(a) the passenger feedback figures following the successful launch of India's first 'Easy Connect' hub-and-spoke international flight model;
(b) whether Government has conducted any feasibility study to extend this integrated international check-in transit model in other Tier-II and Tier-III cities;
(c) if so, the details of the selected airports; 
(d) the number of jobs estimated to be generated by 2030 through the approved modernisation plan for International airports in the country; and
(e) the details and progress of long-term public-private partnership licensing models implemented to upgrade passenger amenities?

(a) the measures taken to strengthen the global competitiveness and export preparedness of India's textile and apparel sector;
(b) the measures taken by Government to address the impact of recent global trade developments, including tariff measures and geopolitical disruptions, on India's textile exports;
(c) the initiatives undertaken, including support under the Rebate of State and Central Taxes and Levies (RoSCTL) Scheme and market diversification efforts, to mitigate such challenges and enhance export competitiveness; and
(d) the strategy adopted to strengthen supply chain resilience, expand India's share in global textile trade and support textile exporters, particularly MSMEs including Maharashtra?

(a) whether CCTV surveillance systems have been installed at railway stations, passenger coaches and other railway premises to enhance passenger safety and security, if so, the total number of railway stations and trains presently covered under CCTV surveillance, zone-wise;
(b) the timeline fixed for extending CCTV coverage to the remaining stations, coaches and trains zone-wise;
(c) whether CCTV footage has assisted in detecting, investigating and preventing thefts, crimes and other security-related incidents during the last three years, if so, the details thereof, year-wise; and
(d) the steps being taken to expand CCTV surveillance across the railway network?

(a) the progress made in the deployment of Kavach 4.0m, including the route kilometres and locomotives covered as of date;
(b) the railway zones and high-density corridors identified for implementation during 2026-27, State & district-wise including Uttar Pradesh;
(c) whether any timeline has been prescribed for network-wise deployment of Kavach, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken to accelerate the installation and commissioning of Kavach across the Indian Railways network?

(a) the objectives and salient provisions of the Scheme to Promote Manufacturing of Electric Passenger Cars in India (SPMEPCI), particularly in the context of attracting investment and promoting domestic manufacturing;
(b) whether the scheme has a provision for the localization of manufacturing and transfer of technology, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the details of the proposed investment, manufacturing capacity, and employment generation under the scheme; and
(d) the framework for the implementation of the scheme, including the role of the Central Government and the participating manufacturers?

(a) whether Government has announced a relief scheme to support exporters affected by disruptions arising from the ongoing West Asian crisis, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the categories of exporters, including MSMEs covered under the scheme and the nature of assistance proposed thereunder;
(c) whether any Inter-Ministerial mechanism has been constituted to monitor supply chain disruptions, shipping routes and logistics challenges, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the other measures taken to safeguard India's exports and minimise the impact of geopolitical disruptions on the export sector?

(a) whether Government is undertaking research and development in advanced nuclear technologies, including Small Modular Reactors (SMRs) and nuclear energy-based green hydrogen production;
(b) if so, the major achievements, pilot projects and technological advancements made, so far;
(c) the estimated contribution of these technologies towards enhancing India's energy security, reducing carbon emissions and achieving the country's net-zero commitments; and
(d) the details of roadmap for their deployment and the benefits likely to accrue to States, including Maharashtra, in terms of clean energy, industrial growth and employment generation?

(a) the progress made in operationalising the Research, Development and Innovation (RDI) fund under the Anusandhan National Research Foundation (ANRF);
(b) the key technology sectors identified for support under the fund, including deep-tech and other strategic sectors;
(c) the measures taken to promote collaboration among academia, industry, startups and research institutions under the fund; and
(d) the funding commitments received and the roadmap for scaling the fund to strengthen India's research, innovation and technology ecosystem?

(a) whether Government has taken note of recent human chain protest in Thane, wherein a large number of citizens, environmental groups and tribal communities demanded protection of forests surrounding the Sanjay Gandhi National Park;
(b) if so, the details thereof and the concerns raised regarding proposed infrastructure and development projects in the area;
(c) whether any assessment has been conducted on the likely impact of such projects on forest cover, biodiversity, wildlife corridors and tribal habitats; and
(d) the measures taken or proposed to balance infrastructure development with ecological conservation and protection of forest-dependent communities?

(a) whether Government has taken cognizance of reports regarding exploitation of women through illegal IVF and sonography centres, particularly in Maharashtra;
(b) if so, State-wise details of complaints received, cases registered, inspections conducted, licences suspended or cancelled and action taken during the last three years, with separate details for Maharashtra;
(c) whether Government has reviewed the implementation of safeguards for protection of women undergoing fertility treatment; and
(d) the measures taken to prevent exploitation and strengthen monitoring and awareness in this regard?

(a) the objectives and key components of the initiative for integrated development of 500 reservoirs and Amrit Sarovars announced in the Union Budget 2026–27;
(b) whether reservoirs and Amrit Sarovars have been identified for implementation of the initiative, if so, the criteria adopted therefor;
(c) the proposed coverage of Fish Farmer Producer Organisations (Fish FPOs), women-led groups and fisheries cooperatives under the initiative; and
(d) the planned investment, including the contribution of the Centre and the States, for implementation of the initiative?

(a) whether the Central Government is aware about Maharashtra’s decision to make Marathi language instruction compulsory from Classes I to X across all educational boards operating in the State;
(b) whether such provisions are consistent with the National Education Policy, 2020 and other relevant educational regulations Governing Central and international boards;
(c) the assistance proposed to be provided for teacher training, curriculum development and learning materials for effective implementation of the policy; and
(d) the mechanisms available for addressing disputes, exemptions or compliance-related issues arising from implementation of the said policy?

(a) the current status of foodgrain procurement, storage and distribution under the Public Distribution System (PDS) and Targeted Public Distribution System (TPDS);
(b) the steps taken to strengthen the One Nation One Ration Card system and digitisation of Fair Price Shops (FPS);
(c) the measures implemented to control food inflation and ensure buffer stock management; and
(d) the impact of these initiatives on overall food security, nutritional outcomes and welfare of vulnerable sections of society?

(a) the details of fertilizer units that remained closed prior to 2014 and have been revived by Government thereafter, unit-wise; 
